a0c39152fbb4e01e704533b","event_uuid":"6afcd89c-d62e-4139-83f4-c44d01a1a7fe","position":{"commit_sha":"490d16d7f0c63a1ad2c860a0cf6e94170d3be895","position":"1788806630939256001-6afcd89c-d62e-4139-83f4-c44d01a1a7fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e5a66805beda2e7de29d68da5518271fd35467e7ccf661d3790d42cc6d78cd35","event_uuid":"e897c85e-061a-4bfb-8032-bf30db14235e","position":{"commit_sha":"4e232a6c969f0030be2bc66dc307986e400873a7","position":"1788807463242376001-e897c85e-061a-4bfb-8032-bf30db14235e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: project goal = mechanisms that don't require exceptions (agents abuse exception paths). The mechanism-ok marker IS the sanctioned no-exception path; if fixing it forces deviation from best practice, escalate.","timestamp":1788761641034997001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD milestone: added RED test tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py::test_mismatch_claim_gate_message_names_sign_review_only; it failed because mismatch still offered review-plan. Implemented verdict-specific reason helper so mismatch names sign-review only while unsigned keeps both remedies. Related targeted tests passed.","timestamp":1788790370717881001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification milestone: full make verify passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset using worktree venv for the verdict-specific claim-gate remedy.","timestamp":1788793135350012001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 2 rebased onto origin/main as 01490836bb42863eb920e178335fbe4547cb60ab and local full make verify passed again. Gerrit CI run 34147719861 then failed only ubuntu-latest py3.13 in tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py::test_rebased_content_equivalent_branch_reports_merged with empty stdout; targeted local reproduction passes and adjacent current-main Gerrit runs passed the same lane. Filed discovered bug buttery-taurine-kinglet for root-cause work rather than hiding the flake. Change remains in review with LLM-Review +1 and Verified -1 pending that unrelated CI issue.","timestamp":1788804146137462001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged Gerrit change 2788 at 2b44cb78c84cd55142263da4945aca1fafbe578f after reasoned recheck of unrelated CI-only feature-branch-inventory failure. Recheck run 34150478213 passed, giving Verified+1; LLM-Review was +1 and the change was submitted. Worktree advanced to the merged Gerrit main revision before close.","timestamp":1788806630939256001}],"created_at":1788570134534418243,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"75c9b209-05ea-48bf-b2d6-44deeb79e7b7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ff4a-2832-def4-4e55"},{"link_uuid":"6fae4aba-bf0e-4323-97bb-00d50e10587a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2969-5c34-05f8-4e78"}],"description":"## Context\n\nCarved out of bug `ff4a-2832-def4-4e55` AC5, which asked that the `--status` / claim-gate refusal\n\"state the CHEAP remedy first and unambiguously, so a reader does not default to re-running a\nbillable review\". Left out of ff4a's fix deliberately: ff4a's change is scoped to the proven root\ncause (the async gate daemon losing the op-cert signer binding) plus its sign-time guard, and this\ntouches a different file with a different rationale.\n\n## The current message and why it hedges\n\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py:141-149` returns both remedies:\n\n> `no certified plan-review attestation (signature: <verdict>; <reason>). Run\n> \\`rebar review-plan <id>\\` to earn one, or \\`rebar sign-review <id>\\` if a review already PASSED\n> but its attestation failed to persist`\n\nThe in-code rationale (bug 94a3) is sound as far as it goes: *\"rebar cannot tell 'never reviewed'\nfrom 'review PASSed but signing aborted' — both leave no record — so name BOTH remedies.\"*\n\n## The improvement — better than a reorder\n\nThat ambiguity is real for `verdict == \"unsigned\"`. It is **not** real for\n`verdict == \"mismatch\"`, which is exactly what ff4a produced:\n\n```\n\"verdict\": \"mismatch\",\n\"reason\": \"... ssh-keygen -Y verify rejected signature (exit 255)\"\n```\n\nA `mismatch` means a signature **exists** and failed to verify. That is unambiguous evidence a\nreview ran and persisted something — so `sign-review` (free, no LLM) is definitively the remedy\nand `review-plan` (15-20 min, billable) is definitively not. Merely reordering the two clauses\nwould still present a choice where none exists.\n\nSo: branch the remedy on `result.get(\"verdict\")` rather than reordering a fixed string.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 - When the signature verdict is `mismatch` (or any verdict that proves a signature was\n      persisted), the refusal names `rebar sign-review <id>` as THE remedy and does not offer\n      `review-plan` as a co-equal alternative.\n- [x] AC2 - When the verdict is `unsigned` the message keeps naming both remedies, preserving the\n      bug 94a3 behaviour and its stated reasoning.\n- [x] AC3 - A test covers both branches by verdict, asserting the observable refusal text.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot removing `sign-review`. Not changing what the gate scores or when it refuses — message only.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest_gate.py","reason":"Branch claim-gate refusal remedy by signature verdict."},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py","reason":"Add RED-first coverage for mismatch vs unsigned remedy text."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2969-5c34-05f8-4e78"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f20c9bea-b51d-406a-9927-fded0aa3985b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3f5a-2ea8-7041-42a6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Branch the plan-review claim-gate remedy on the signature verdict: a mismatch proves a review happened, so name sign-review unambiguously","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c1f862c3-60de-480c-a37e-1abd71a48c6e","104a7dee-ee4b-4ec0-b6a0-04e1341b3e67","f20c9bea-b51d-406a-9927-fded0aa3985b","7a6cd9fa-f3f6-497d-a537-0c0132f90682","29f6fa32-4c53-4602-9758-4d6a23473a35","1ba6fdab-ff45-48b5-ba49-945e58519ca1","3cb1ff12-2f8f-414e-96ce-b12ba60bf464","6fae4aba-bf0e-4323-97bb-00d50e10587a","a74a0bed-70a3-4eb2-b579-f2c08dbeeca4","89b9594d-7a29-47bb-ab41-eb04338bef2c","6afcd89c-d62e-4139-83f4-c44d01a1a7fe","e897c85e-061a-4bfb-8032-bf30db14235e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788807463242376002,"uuid":"e9835e6e-c066-4325-9024-7a498a606712"}